# WildFire test run, 2026-09-16 — the full planned configuration, both receivers.
#
# No --freq and no --rate: the profile decides. uhf rotates 466.0 (300 s) and
# 446.0 (60 s); vhf rotates 146.0 and 154.95 (180 s each); both at 10 MSPS.
# This combination — two radios, rotation, 10 MSPS together — had never run on
# hardware before this commit.
#
# 10 MSPS with Gate 2 unpassed, deliberately. In Boston it ran 26% short against
# ~11,000 events/hour of mostly periodic business telemetry. A rural camp should
# carry far less, and whether 10 MSPS keeps up at a real event is the question
# the deployment needs answered. Overflows are counted in the journal stats.
#
# Both receivers share one database, as designed: receiver_id tells them apart,
# WAL plus busy_timeout handles the two writers. Audio budget is per process.
RFSURVEY_DB=data/wildfire.sqlite
# Its OWN capture directory, not data/captures. CaptureStore writes to
# <capture-dir>/run<N>/<event id>.wav, and both run and event ids restart at 1
# in every new database — so WildFire's run 4 in data/captures would have
# written into the same directory as Phase 4's run 4 (912,328 files) and
# overwritten them by event number. Caught 2026-09-16 before any overlap.
RFSURVEY_ARGS=--capture-dir data/captures/wildfire --capture-mb 40000
